!}

= El alijo

[? if ch_res = "bien" : It is there, and it is real, and the column stands around it for a moment in a kind of silence. [? if aid_tipo = "armas" : Crates. Actual crates, with actual grease on the actual rifles inside them, and ammunition measured in cases rather than in rounds counted out of a man's pocket. ?][? if aid_tipo = "cuadros" : Two people who have done this in two other countries, and a load of matériel, and within a month the column is doing things correctly that it has been doing approximately for three years. ?][? if aid_tipo = "dinero" : A great deal of money, in a country where money buys rifles, boots, doctors, silence and trucks. ?] It took months and a march across the state on somebody else's schedule and it was worth every day of it. ?][? if ch_res = "parcial" : You get to it and you get some of it out, and you leave the rest because the alternative was a firefight over crates in the open. [? if aid_tipo = "armas" : Half the weapons come up the mountain and half of them are in an army inventory by Friday, which will be photographed and shown on television as proof of the foreign hand. ?][? if aid_tipo = "cuadros" : One of the two instructors comes out with you. The other does not, and he was not Mexican, which is going to be a story. ?][? if aid_tipo = "dinero" : You get most of it. Most is a great deal. ?] ?][? if ch_res = "mal" : They were there before you. Of course they were — a shipment has to be arranged by people who talk to other people, and a coastline has a navy on it, and you marched a whole column across the state on a fixed schedule to a fixed point, which is the one thing a guerrilla must never do and the one thing collecting a shipment absolutely requires. You lose four people getting off that ground and you lose the load entirely, and within a week the Secretaría is displaying it to the press as evidence of an international conspiracy against Mexico, which — inconveniently, in this instance — is more or less what it was. ?]

- @cat_politica: Continuar.

@pol_pcm
face-image: img/pcmconf.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.pol_pcm+=12; if(Q.pol_pcm>100){Q.pol_pcm=100;} Q.unity=(Q.unity||0)+4; Q.political_capital=(Q.political_capital||0)+3; Q.pcm_canal=1; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; if(Q.linea_guerra>=12){Q.pol_pcm-=6; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-2;} !}

You send someone down to the Party — the PCM, legal-ish, cautious, sitting on the one thing the sierra does not have: a national political apparatus and a name the whole left recognizes. The conversation is old and unfinished: they think the gun is adventurism that will bring the state down on everyone; you think their patience is a chair in an antechamber. But the channel matters. It means the movement is not a bandit gang in the papers, it means cadre and lawyers and printing, and it means that when the moment comes to convert the war into politics, there is somebody to convert it *with*. They will want their price — a say over the line. Everyone always does.

- @cat_politica: Continuar.

@pol_intl
face-image: img/solidarity.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.pol_intl+=14; if(Q.pol_intl>100){Q.pol_intl=100;} Q.legitimidad_regimen-=4; Q.internac_armada=(Q.internac_armada||0)+1; Q.expediente=(Q.expediente||0)+3; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; if(Q.presos>0){Q.presos-=1;} !}

You get the war out of the country: the testimonies smuggled to exiles and foreign journalists, the disappeared named at conferences the Mexican government pays good money to be respectable at, the solidarity committees in Paris and Havana and Berkeley reading the list aloud. Mexico's rulers can survive almost anything except being *seen* — the regime that sells itself abroad as the gentle revolutionary republic cannot afford photographs of its own airbase. It buys the prisoners a little safety, because a named man is harder to disappear, and it costs you another page in a file that is already long.

- @cat_politica: Continuar.

@pue_escuela
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.f_pueblo_mes=(Q.f_pueblo_mes||0)+1; var _n=Q.f_pueblo_mes; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(4,_h*0.24)/_n; Q.f_cerco+=4+(_n-1)*11; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+2; Q.zona_gobernada=1; Q.f_moral+=2; !}

Literacy circles under a tree, the médico's rounds through the hamlets, a school where the state built none in fifty years. This is the part of the war that has nothing to do with rifles and decides it anyway: the sierra learns that where the guerrilla governs, a child can read and a fever can be treated — that the movement is not merely against something but *for* a way of living. Che called it the guerrilla's obligation; Lucio simply called it being a teacher, which is what he was before any of this.

- @cat_pueblo: Continuar.

@m_campamento
face-image: img/guerillacamp.webp
view-if: f_campamento = 0
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2 and apoyo_popular >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: A permanent base costs 2 action points and needs real water around it (apoyo 35+) — a camp the villages will not cover is a camp the army finds in a week.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=2; Q.f_campamento=1; Q.camp_nodo=Q.col_nodo; Q.camp_nivel=1; Q.camp_visto=0; Q.f_moral+=8; Q.f_comida+=10; Q.zona_gobernada=1; Q.f_cerco+=4; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} !}

You stop running long enough to build. In a fold of the sierra the villages will not talk about, the column raises the thing every guerrilla army eventually needs and every guerrilla manual warns about: a **campamento base** — ramadas under the canopy, a store of maize and salt, a cache for the parque, a lean-to that will be the hospital, a fire that can burn after dark because the ridges above are watched by people who love you.

It changes the war. A band with a home can rest wounded instead of carrying them, can cache instead of hauling, can train recruits properly, and can come back to something. It also gives the enemy the one thing you have denied him for years: *an address.* Everything fixed can be found. Keep the water deep and the ring loose, and the camp is your strength. Let either rot, and it becomes the place where the column dies all at once instead of a few at a time.

- @cat_movimiento: Continuar.

@m_mejorar
view-if: f_campamento = 1
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1 and camp_nivel < 3
unavailable-subtitle: You need the base built (and not already at its full extent) to deepen it.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.camp_nivel+=1; Q.f_moral+=5; Q.f_comida+=8; Q.apoyo_popular+=4; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+3; if(Q.camp_nivel>=2){Q.f_medico=1;} !}

The camp deepens into something that begins to look less like a hiding place and more like a small free country. [? if camp_nivel = 2 : A proper hospital under a thatch roof, with the médico's instruments boiled in a pot — the wounded stop being a death sentence and start being patients. ?][? if camp_nivel >= 3 : A school, a workshop that reloads cartridges, drying racks, a printing frame for the communiqués — the base has become the capital of a country of about four hundred people, and everyone in the sierra knows how to find it and no one will say. ?] Every improvement makes the column harder to starve and harder to break. Every improvement also makes it harder to abandon.

- @cat_movimiento: Continuar.

@m_volver_campo
view-if: f_campamento = 1
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; if(Q.camp_nodo){Q.col_nodo=Q.camp_nodo; Q['sn_'+Q.camp_nodo]=1;} var _n=Q.camp_nivel||1; Q.f_comida+=10+_n*6; Q.f_moral+=6+_n*3; Q.f_parque+=4+_n*3; if(Q.f_bajas>0){Q.f_bajas-=1;} if(_n>=2&&Q.f_hombres<60){Q.f_hombres+=1;} Q.f_cerco+=6; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} !}

The column comes home. Whatever else the war is, for a week it is hot food, a dry place to sleep, the wounded handed to someone whose job is keeping them alive, and the parque counted out of the cache instead of scraped from the dead. Men who were a week from walking away remember why they are here. The march resumes with fuller bellies and heavier packs.

And every road that leads home also leads *here*, which is why coming back always costs a little in the one currency the sierra measures: the ring drawn a notch tighter around the one place the army knows you keep returning to.

- @cat_movimiento: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# EL CERCO — the encirclement. Fires as an event when the ring closes. Escape, or bleed.
# =====================================================================
@cerco
title: El cerco
