= El cerco

It is the oldest way a foco dies, and this morning it is yours: the army has concentrated, the roads are blocked, the helicopters quarter the ridgelines, and the ring you let tighten is now a closed circle with your column inside it. This is the moment Bolivia turned on — the moment Lucio's turned on, in the end. The water decides it now. If the people are with you, someone is already climbing to warn you of the gap. If they are not, someone has already climbed down to tell the captain where you sleep.

- @cerco_agua: **Confiar en el agua.** Trust the villages to show you the gap — slip out the way only people who love you would know. *(needs deep apoyo; clean escape if the water is with you)*
- @cerco_montana: **Reventar hacia lo alto.** Break uphill, ditch the heavy loads, outclimb the ring where the trucks cannot go. *(costs comida + parque; escapes by distance, not by love)*
- @cerco_pelear: **Romper el cerco a tiros.** Fight through the thinnest point. *(a battle — win and you wound the army; lose and the column is gutted)*

@cerco_agua
on-arrival: {! if(Q.apoyo_popular>=50){Q.f_cerco=15;Q.f_moral+=6;Q.apoyo_popular-=3;}else{Q.f_cerco=45;Q.f_hombres-=3;Q.f_moral-=6;Q.f_bajas+=3;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+1;} !}

[? if apoyo_popular >= 50 : A boy you taught to read comes up the arroyo before dawn and takes you out through a draw the army did not know was there, because the army does not know this country and the boy was born in it. The ring closes on empty ground. This is the whole thesis of the thing — the fish, the water — proven in one grey morning. ?][? if apoyo_popular < 50 : You wait for the warning that does not come, because the water is too thin to carry it, and by the time you move on your own the gap is a killing ground. The column claws out with holes in it. The sea was not deep enough, and men paid the difference. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

@cerco_montana
choose-if: f_comida >= 15
unavailable-subtitle: An uphill break needs food in the men — at least 15 comida.
on-arrival: {! Q.col_nodo="elotatal"; Q.f_cerco=20; Q.f_comida-=15; Q.f_parque-=6; Q.f_moral-=3; Q.f_hombres-=1; !}

You dump the caches you cannot carry, take the highest, cruelest ground, and outclimb the ring where no truck and few soldiers will follow. It works because exhaustion is cheaper than capture — you buy your lives with the loads you leave behind and the men's legs. The circle closes on abandoned kit and cold ashes. You are deep in the sierra now, safe and stripped, and the rebuilding starts again from less.

- @root: Continuar.

@cerco_pelear
on-arrival: {! Q.f_parque-=10; if(Q.f_parque<0){Q.f_parque=0;} var _r=(Q.f_hombres*0.5)+(Q.f_moral*0.35)+(Q.apoyo_popular*0.2)-70+(Math.random()*40-20); if(_r>=0){Q.f_cerco=25;Q.f_desgaste+=12;Q.f_moral+=6;Q.f_hombres-=2;Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2;Q.legitimidad_regimen-=3;}else{Q.f_cerco=40;Q.f_hombres-=6;Q.f_moral-=12;Q.f_bajas+=6;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+2;} !}

You pick the thinnest arc of the ring and throw the column at it. [? if f_moral >= 55 and f_hombres >= 18 : The thin point gives — you punch through, bloody the army at the gap, and are gone into the trees before it can close again. A ring broken from the inside is a humiliation the garrison feels for months. ?][? if f_moral < 55 or f_hombres < 18 : The thin point was thin for a reason — a baited gap, machine guns on the flanks. You get out because you have to, dragging the wounded, leaving too many. The ring did what rings are for. ?]

- @root: Continuar.
